<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Badge @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</PageTitle>
<GoTo LabelText="Badge API reference & usage page title" />
<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Badge @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>



<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-badge</span> CSS class: the BEM classes it provides, the strongly-typed <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Badge</span> C# object
    used to apply them, supporting enums, and the CSS variables used for styling.
</p>

<h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-badge</span> is a small, static label - a status, a count, a category. It is <b>not interactive</b>: it has no hover, active or focus styling and does not look or behave like a control.
    If you need something that can be clicked, use <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Button</span> or <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Link</span> instead.
</p>
<p>
    With no modifiers, a badge is the small size, with a transparent background, a border and a fixed border radius of 3. <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-badge</span> is not part of a radius group and has its own
    independent radius settings, so a theme change does not alter it - use <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">FixedRadius</span> to choose a different value. Every badge has a border so that badges with and without a scheme
    stay the same size.
</p>
<p>
    Colours are theme-reactive: they're built from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-cls-*</span> variables described below, which in turn derive from the same <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-*</span> primitives used across every
    Blazor Ramp component. Changing your theme updates <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-badge</span> automatically - no separate configuration needed.
</p>
<p>
    To place an icon in a badge, add an <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">SvgIcon</span> element with <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-hidden="true"</span>. The <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Small</span> and <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Regular</span> icon sizes fit within a badge's line height; the
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Large</span> and <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">ExtraLarge</span> sizes will make the badge taller. To change the space between an icon and the badge text, use the shared <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Gap</span> utility classes.
</p>
<p>
    A badge must never rely on colour alone to convey meaning - always include text. If the visible text is ambiguous without context (a bare "3", for example), add visually hidden text
    such as "unread messages". Use visually hidden text rather than <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-label</span> here, because a plain <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">&lt;span&gt;</span> has no role for an accessible name to be applied to, so
    assistive technologies may ignore it.
</p>

<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="mobile-centred-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Badge</span> provides the BEM CSS classes for the br-badge block: an inline, static label that can hold text and an icon.
    </p>
    <section>
        <h3 id="badge-class" class="mobile-centred-heading">Badge class</h3>
        <div class="@Section.Base @Section.NoPadding @Section.OverflowX(UnitScroll.Auto) @Padding.Block(UnitSpace.Four)">
            <table class="@Table.Base @Table.CodeTable" tabindex="0" aria-labelledby="badge-class">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th scope="col">Return</th>
                        <th scope="col">Const/Static Method</th>
                        <th scope="col">Description</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Badge.Base</td>
                        <td>The base class, <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-badge</span>. Always required.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Badge.TransparentBorder</td>
                        <td>Makes the border transparent (looks like its removed) so there is no size change.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Badge.Size(BadgeSize badgeSize)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets the badge's size.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme solidScheme)</td>
                        <td>Gets the class that sets the badge's solid colour scheme: its background, border, and a contrasting text colour.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td>string</td>
                        <td>Badge.FixedRadius(UnitRadius unitRadius)</td>
                        <td>Gets the modifier class that sets the badge's border radius to a fixed unit value in place of the default.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </section>
</section>

