<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Usage</h2>
    <p>
        The following shows examples of the styles applied to badges.
        <b>Note: </b>All of the CSS classes have variables for both light and dark schemes. Click the Theme button at the top of the page.
    </p>
    <p>
        Below shows styling the badge using its default size of small without any scheme so the default styles are applied.
    </p>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CssClassesSnippets.Badge_Small_Default_Example" AriaLabel="Badge default styling code example" />
    <p>
        <span class="@Badge.Base">Default Badge</span>
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong> all badges do have a border to keep sizes even, that can be removed (made transparent). By default every badge size has a fixed border radius of 3 which
        can be changed.
    </p>
    <h3>Default styling</h3>
    <p>
        All badges are bordered with transparent a background with a fixed border radius of 3 unless changed.
        In the examples below I changed the border radius of the large badge to 5, the large badge had its radius increased to 5, 
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">class="@@Badge.Base @@Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Large) @@Badge.FixedRadius(UnitRadius.Five)"</span>
    </p>
    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <span type="button" class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Tiny)">Tiny Badge</span>
        <span type="button" class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Small)">Small Badge</span>
        <span type="button" class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Medium)">Medium Badge</span>
        <span type="button" class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Large) @Badge.FixedRadius(UnitRadius.Five)">Large Badge</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Fixed central unit colour value from each of the colour palettes</h3>
    <p>
        Excluding the inverted scheme, the colour of the text for these are set via the CSS <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">contrast-color</span> function.
        To add a colour scheme you just the scheme you want, for example <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">class="@@Badge.Base @@Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Primary)"</span>
    </p>
    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Primary)">Primary Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Neutral)">Neutral Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Secondary)">Secondary Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Accent)">Accent Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Danger)">Danger Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Warning)">Warning Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Success)">Success Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Info)">Info Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.Inverted)">Inverted Badge</span>
    </div>

    <h3>Uses the lighter shade with a darker text of the same colour from each colour palette</h3>

    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.PrimaryLighter)">Primary Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.NeutralLighter)">Neutral Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.SecondaryLighter)">Secondary Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.AccentLighter)">Accent Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.DangerLighter)">Danger Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.WarningLighter)">Warning Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.SuccessLighter)">Success Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoLighter)">Info Lighter Badge</span>

    </div>
    <h3>Uses the lighter shade with a darker text of the same colour from each colour palette with the border made transparent</h3>
    <p>
        To make the badge look like it has not border we make it transparent for example 
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">class="@@Badge.Base @@Badge.TransparentBorder @@Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.PrimaryLighter)"</span>
    </p>
    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.PrimaryLighter)">Primary Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.NeutralLighter)">Neutral Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.SecondaryLighter)">Secondary Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.AccentLighter)">Accent Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.DangerLighter)">Danger Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.WarningLighter)">Warning Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.SuccessLighter)">Success Lighter Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.TransparentBorder @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoLighter)">Info Lighter Badge</span>

    </div>
    <h3>Uses a darker shade with a lighter text of the same colour from each colour palette</h3>

    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.PrimaryDarker)">Primary Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.NeutralDarker)">Neutral Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.SecondaryDarker)">Secondary Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.AccentDarker)">Accent Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.DangerDarker)">Danger Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.WarningDarker)">Warning Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.SuccessDarker)">Success Darker Badge</span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoDarker)">Info Darker Badge</span>
    </div>
    
    <h3>
        Adding icons to badges
    </h3>
    <p>
        Just like the buttons you can add icons to badges with or without text, if you use icons ensure you add the appropriate ARIA attributes 
        dependant on the context.
    </p>
    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoDarker) @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Tiny)">
            <span class="@SvgIcon.Base @SvgIcon.Size(UnitIconSize.Small)" style="--_svg-icon-source:var(--svg-nuget-icon)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            NuGet Badge
        </span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoDarker) @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Small)">
            <span class="@SvgIcon.Base @SvgIcon.Size(UnitIconSize.Regular)" style="--_svg-icon-source:var(--svg-nuget-icon)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            NuGet Badge
        </span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoDarker) @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Medium)">
            <span class="@SvgIcon.Base @SvgIcon.Size(UnitIconSize.Regular)" style="--_svg-icon-source:var(--svg-nuget-icon)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            NuGet Badge
        </span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoDarker) @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Large)">
            <span class="@SvgIcon.Base @SvgIcon.Size(UnitIconSize.Regular)" style="--_svg-icon-source:var(--svg-nuget-icon)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            NuGet Badge
        </span>
        <span class="@Badge.Base @Badge.Scheme(BadgeSolidScheme.InfoDarker) @Badge.Size(BadgeSize.Large)" aria-label="NuGet badge">
            <span class="@SvgIcon.Base @SvgIcon.Size(UnitIconSize.Regular)" style="--_svg-icon-source:var(--svg-nuget-icon)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </span>
    </div>
    <p>
        Code for the above
    </p>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CssClassesSnippets.Badge_Icons_Example" AriaLabel="Badge with icon code example." />
</section>

